; WaveSmithInstall -- the package's Installer at the NOVICE level (no
; questions: SYS:Tools/WaveSmith, the GlowIcons), its pages clicked by
; DEV:Test/InstallClicks (grabs DEV:Test/install-<tag>-<n>.ppm). The staged
; package is DEV:Release (gmake release-drawer; `gmake autotest` makes it).
; A: as the disk is (AHI installed): the closing page without the notice;
; what was installed copied back to DEV:Test/Installed, which
; test/auto/WaveSmithInstall.check compares with the package byte for
; byte; the drawers opened on Workbench and grabbed, with the GlowIcons and
; then the classic icons (DEV:Test/WSDrawers.rexx: arranged-<set>-<n>.ppm);
; then deleted from the test disk's copy.
; B: once more with DEVS:ahi.device hidden (and no prisma.library on the
; test disk): the closing page carries the notice, the installation goes on.
;   gmake autotest T=WaveSmithInstall W=rtg32 LIMIT=300
FailAt 21
Wait 10
If NOT EXISTS DEV:Release/WaveSmith/Install
  Echo >DEV:Test/auto.log "SKIPPED: no DEV:Release (gmake release-drawer)"
  Echo >DEV:Test/AutoDone done
  Quit
EndIf
Delete >NIL: SYS:Tools/WaveSmith SYS:Tools/WaveSmith.info ALL QUIET
Delete >NIL: DEV:Test/install-w-#? DEV:Test/install-x-#? DEV:Test/arranged-#? DEV:Test/Installed DEV:Test/Installed.info ALL QUIET
; a run that died in B left AHI hidden
If EXISTS DEVS:ahi.device.away
  Rename >NIL: DEVS:ahi.device.away DEVS:ahi.device
EndIf
Echo >DEV:Test/auto.log "WaveSmithInstall"
List >>DEV:Test/auto.log DEVS:ahi.device LFORMAT "  A with %P%N"
Delete >NIL: RAM:WSInstallDone RAM:WSInstallDone2 QUIET
Stack 20000
; every (source) is relative to the unpacked drawer, which Workbench makes
; the current one for a double-clicked Install icon; the pages clicked by
; DEV:Test/InstallClicks, the Installer in the foreground
CD DEV:Release/WaveSmith
Run >NIL: Execute DEV:Test/InstallClicks RAM:WSInstallDone w
FailAt 100
SYS:System/Installer SCRIPT DEV:Release/WaveSmith/Install APPNAME WaveSmith MINUSER NOVICE DEFUSER NOVICE NOPRETEND NOLOG
Echo >>DEV:Test/auto.log "  Installer RC $RC (0 = it reached its own (exit) page)"
FailAt 21
Echo >RAM:WSInstallDone "done"
CD SYS:
Wait 8
Echo >>DEV:Test/auto.log "installed:"
List >>DEV:Test/auto.log SYS:Tools/WaveSmith ALL LFORMAT "  %P%N %L"
List >>DEV:Test/auto.log SYS:Tools/WaveSmith.info LFORMAT "  %P%N %L"
; the arrangement (tools/arrange_drawers.py) on Workbench: SYS:Tools and
; every drawer installed, grabbed (arranged-glow-<n>.ppm); then the classic
; icons, copied over as the Installer copies them when they are chosen --
; after the copy back, so the .check still sees what a novice gets
RX DEV:Test/WSDrawers.rexx glow
Copy SYS:Tools/WaveSmith DEV:Test/Installed ALL CLONE QUIET
Copy SYS:Tools/WaveSmith.info DEV:Test/Installed.info CLONE QUIET
Copy DEV:Release/WaveSmith/Files/WaveSmith/WaveSmith.info SYS:Tools/WaveSmith/WaveSmith.info CLONE QUIET
Copy DEV:Release/WaveSmith/Files/WaveSmith.info SYS:Tools/WaveSmith.info CLONE QUIET
RX DEV:Test/WSDrawers.rexx classic
Delete >NIL: SYS:Tools/WaveSmith SYS:Tools/WaveSmith.info ALL QUIET

; B: without AHI (hidden for this run, put back after): the closing page
; says WaveSmith has nothing to play through (install-x-<n>: the notice)
Echo >>DEV:Test/auto.log "B: without AHI"
Rename >NIL: DEVS:ahi.device DEVS:ahi.device.away
CD DEV:Release/WaveSmith
Run >NIL: Execute DEV:Test/InstallClicks RAM:WSInstallDone2 x
FailAt 100
SYS:System/Installer SCRIPT DEV:Release/WaveSmith/Install APPNAME WaveSmith MINUSER NOVICE DEFUSER NOVICE NOPRETEND NOLOG
Echo >>DEV:Test/auto.log "  Installer RC $RC"
FailAt 21
Echo >RAM:WSInstallDone2 "done"
CD SYS:
Rename >NIL: DEVS:ahi.device.away DEVS:ahi.device
Wait 8
List >>DEV:Test/auto.log SYS:Tools/WaveSmith/WaveSmith DEVS:ahi.device LFORMAT "  %P%N"
Delete >NIL: SYS:Tools/WaveSmith SYS:Tools/WaveSmith.info ALL QUIET
Echo >DEV:Test/AutoDone done
